Search each base-font directory only once in GlobalParams::setupBaseFonts().

findFontFile() calls setupBaseFonts(POPPLER_FONTSDIR) on every font lookup.
Without the base-14 font files installed, every call tried to open all 14 fonts
in the given directory and in each of the five displayFontDirs again, and
logged "No display font" for each. Remember the directories already searched
and return early for them; a font missing from all of them stays missing.

No regression test: this is a performance fix and changes no result. For the
repro (one page using 16 fonts), the wasm32 poppler-pdf fuzz target runs ~15.5M
instructions with the fix and ~281M without (native ASan build: 0.22 s vs
0.67 s). poppler-page_search also needs more than 20M without the fix and less
with it; poppler-doc and poppler-page_label stay below 20M either way.

Not fixed upstream as of 9182fd5.
Upstream: none found (poppler/poppler issues and MRs searched for
setupBaseFonts, findFontFile, base fonts).

diff --git a/poppler/GlobalParams.cc b/poppler/GlobalParams.cc
index ad43d0f..3f82902 100644
--- a/poppler/GlobalParams.cc
+++ b/poppler/GlobalParams.cc
@@ -1374,6 +1374,12 @@ void GlobalParams::setupBaseFonts(const char *dir)
     FILE *f;
     int i, j;
 
+    // findFontFile() calls this for every font lookup; without the base fonts installed,
+    // each call probed all 14 fonts in every directory again
+    if (!baseFontDirsSearched.insert(dir ? dir : "").second) {
+        return;
+    }
+
     for (i = 0; displayFontTab[i].name; ++i) {
         if (fontFiles.count(displayFontTab[i].name) > 0) {
             continue;
